  "content": {
    "id": "p50-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "Show that $x^2-4px+(4p^2-0)=0$ always has integer solutions for all integer $p$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\Delta=0$, so the repeated root is $x=2p$, an integer for every integer $p$.",
      "worked": "$a=1$, $b=-4p$, $c=4p^2$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=(-4p)^2-4(1)(4p^2)\\\\\\Delta&=16p^2-16p^2\\\\\\Delta&=0\\end{align*}$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{4p\\pm\\sqrt{0}}{2}\\\\x&=2p\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe roots are equal. Since $p$ is an integer, $2p$ is an integer.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 47
  },
